# Local development reads both tokens from .env (git-ignored). `make run` and
# `make dev-env` create it with random tokens, or add a missing one.
# GANTRY_TOKEN is for API clients (bearer), GANTRY_UI_TOKEN for the web
# login; they must differ. Generate each with `openssl rand -hex 24`; the
# agent refuses tokens shorter than 24 characters.
GANTRY_TOKEN=
GANTRY_UI_TOKEN=

# Single sign-on for the web UI (optional; see "Single sign-on" in the
# README). Needs GANTRY_PUBLIC_URL and an allow list.
# GANTRY_PUBLIC_URL=https://gantry.example.com
# GANTRY_OIDC_ISSUER=https://auth.example.com/application/o/gantry/
# GANTRY_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# GANTRY_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GANTRY_OIDC_ALLOWED_GROUPS=gantry-admins
